# Copy this file to .env.local (already gitignored — never commit that file) and
# uncomment/edit whatever you need. Vite loads .env.local automatically, with
# higher priority than any committed .env file, and it is never bundled into a
# production build.

# ── Kadena node override (local dev only) ──────────────────────────────────
# The shipped/production default (KADENA_MAINNET_DEFAULT_NODE_URL in
# packages/codex-ouronet/src/kadena/kadenaReads.ts) points at our own node via
# its DuckDNS hostname. That hostname resolves to the node's PUBLIC IP, and the
# LAN router the node sits behind will not loop that traffic back to a machine
# on the same LAN (a "hairpin NAT" limitation, confirmed 2026-09-27) -- so if
# you are developing on the same LAN as the node, every Kadena balance read
# will hang/fail until you point at the node's LAN-reachable address instead.
#
# Uncomment and set this to get past that WITHOUT editing the shipped default:
#   VITE_KADENA_NODE_URL=http://localhost:31849
# or, from another machine on the same LAN:
#   VITE_KADENA_NODE_URL=http://<node's LAN IP>:31849
#
# Leave this unset if you are NOT on the node's own LAN -- the shipped default
# already works fine from anywhere else, including a normal dev machine.
# VITE_KADENA_NODE_URL=
